


== standard InChI (the key today): tautomers MERGE, isomers SPLIT, Ar states UNIFY ==
  Ar   (u0 p4)       skel = InChI=1S/Ar
  Ar*  (u2 p3)       skel = InChI=1S/Ar
  2-pyridone         skel = InChI=1S/C5H5NO/c7-5-3-1-2-4-6-5/h1-4H,(H,6,7)
  2-hydroxypyridine  skel = InChI=1S/C5H5NO/c7-5-3-1-2-4-6-5/h1-4H,(H,6,7)
  DME  (COC)         skel = InChI=1S/C2H6O/c1-3-2/h1-2H3
  ethanol (CCO)      skel = InChI=1S/C2H6O/c1-2-3/h3H,2H2,1H3
  -> pyridone and hydroxypyridine share a key (tautomer merge); DME != ethanol; Ar == Ar*

== FixedH separates the tautomer NEUTRALS but its /f sits BEHIND /q,/p on IONS ==
  neutral 2-pyridone       FixedH: InChI=1/C5H5NO/c7-5-3-1-2-4-6-5/h1-4H,(H,6,7)/f/h6H
  neutral 2-hydroxypyridine FixedH: InChI=1/C5H5NO/c7-5-3-1-2-4-6-5/h1-4H,(H,6,7)/f/h7H
  cation  pyridinium (proton) FixedH: InChI=1/C5H4NO/c7-5-3-1-2-4-6-5/h1-4H/p+1/fC5H5NO/h6H/q+1
  cation  formamide+ (radical) FixedH: InChI=1/CH3NO/c2-1-3/h1H,2H2/q+1
  -> on the cations /p and /f precede /q and the main formula shifts, so truncating
     at /q,/p to make the key charge-independent DROPS /f. FixedH cannot be the
